  <class_name>ExportModelToSpeckle</class_name>
  <display_name>Export Model to Speckle</display_name>
  <description>Publishes the model's geometry and energy-model inputs (constructions, U-values, space types, internal loads, thermal zones, HVAC assignment) to a Speckle project as a new version, so it can be viewed, compared and analysed alongside other design models. The OpenStudio model is not changed.</description>
  <modeler_description>Surfaces, sub-surfaces, interior partitions and shading surfaces are triangulated in site coordinates (metres, north axis applied) and sent with the specklepy 2026.9+ bundle API (BundleBuilder + operations.send3). Objects are organised Building &gt; Story &gt; Space, linked to Speckle levels, rooms (spaces), hosts (sub-surface -&gt; parent surface), groups (thermal zones) and systems (air loops). specklepy is loaded from the OpenStudio embedded Python (add its folder with the python_packages_path argument) or, failing that, an external Python 3.11+ interpreter given by external_python. A JSON payload of everything sent is always written to the run directory. The token is read from the speckle_token argument, else the SPECKLE_TOKEN environment variable, else a local Speckle desktop-connector account.</modeler_description>
